@page "/components/menus"

<PageTitle>Menus — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">Context menu, menubar, navigation menu</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    Three menus that are not a dropdown, and differ from it in exactly one way each: what opens
    them, how you move between them, and what they contain.
</p>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Context menu</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    One <code>contextmenu</code> listener covers the right button, the context-menu key and a long
    press on touch — the platform fires the same event for all three. A right-click handler on a
    div gets only the first, which is how context menus end up unreachable by keyboard.
</p>
<Example Source="ContextMenuExample.razor"><ContextMenuExample /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Menubar</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    Once any menu is open, hovering another opens that one instead of doing nothing. That is what
    makes a menubar feel like a menubar, and it is the only part of it that is not free.
</p>
<Example Source="MenubarExample.razor"><MenubarExample /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Navigation menu</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    A <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code> around a real <code>&lt;ul&gt;</code>. Radix animates every panel
    through one shared viewport so they cross-fade; each panel here is its own popover in the top
    layer instead — no cross-fade, and in exchange nothing clips it and there is no z-index to
    lose. Put <code>[up-nav]</code> on it and Unpoly marks the current link.
</p>
<Example Source="NavigationMenuExample.razor"><NavigationMenuExample /></Example>
